// Deductions -- WIRE-8 (26.09.2026, DECISION-0379 Д-22 item (б), implemented_unverified).
//
// Lower packages (`gross_income`, `income_individual`) declare local contracts for deductions this package owns and cannot import
// this package (it imports both; a direct import back would be an import cycle). The owner therefore DERIVES the lower package's
// `pub` relation from its own relation with a qualified rule head (same technique as `pub-interface-wiring.law`, Д-13 item 5). The
// case-fact channel stays valid: scenarios of the lower packages never load this package. Nothing is restated or recomputed.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.deductions version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:deductions:clir";

use self::{
    Person,
    TaxableYear,
    nol_deduction,
};

// --- section 62(a) above-the-line slots: strict auto-derivation REMOVED (26.09.2026, JUDGMENT CALL, TECH-GAPS G498) ---
//
// The three bridge rules that derived gross-income's section 62(a)(11)/(15)/(16)
// slots (§194 reforestation, §217 moving, §220 Archer MSA) from `deduction_allowed`
// stood here and were deleted together with the four bridges in
// `pub-interface-wiring.law` (§219/§221/§223/§162). They closed the predicate
// cycle `above_the_line_deduction_amount -> deduction_allowed ->
// adjusted_gross_income -> above_the_line_deduction_amount` (§110/§103): the AGI
// rule sums the slots in a head term — a completion edge under every wrapper
// (E-0112) — so no `supported(P)` monotone channel could legalize it. The slot
// amounts are case-asserted dependency contracts; the §194/§217/§220 norms
// themselves are untouched (their `deduction_allowed` conclusions stay).

// --- section 56(a)(4): the regular-tax net operating loss deduction read by the alternative minimum tax ---------------------------

rule W8RegularNolDeductionForAmt(p: Person, y: TaxableYear, amount: Money) strict {
    label en official "section 56(a)(4): the net operating loss deduction allowed under section 172 in computing the regular tax is this package's section 172 deduction";
    when nol_deduction(p, y, amount);
    then us.irc.income_individual::regular_net_operating_loss_deduction(p, y, amount);
}
